From 1eaa23fa9e80f8b96502fafebe241850db597c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:55:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/73] input: touchscreen: focaltech: Register the MSM DRM
 notifier

The driver picks its display-blank notifier with

    #if defined(CONFIG_FB) ... #elif defined(CONFIG_DRM) ...

This kernel has CONFIG_FB=y and CONFIG_DRM=y while the display is MSM DRM
(SDE), so the legacy fb_notifier was registered - and an MSM DRM display never
fires FB blank events (it calls msm_drm_notifier_call_chain() from
msm_atomic.c).  fts_ts_suspend()/fts_ts_resume(), whose only callers are those
callbacks, were therefore never called, and the i2c driver has no dev_pm_ops
either (FTS_PATCH_COMERR_PM == 0).

With the screen off the touch controller stayed awake with its IRQ enabled:
the threaded handler ran continuously doing i2c reads (constant CPU wakeups,
i.e. the system becoming very laggy after locking) and whatever it read was
reported as touch points (erratic touch reports).

Discriminate on CONFIG_FB_MSM like st/fts.c in this tree and register the MSM
DRM client like hxchipset/himax_common.c.  Also fixes the matching header
include (linux/msm_drm_notify.h was only reachable in the dead CONFIG_DRM_PANEL
branch) and selects the MSM_DRM event variant of drm_notifier_callback.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../focaltech_touch/focaltech_core.c          |  64 ++++---
 .../0001-focaltech-msm-drm-notifier.patch     | 178 ++++++++++++++++++
 s6patch触摸/README.md                       | 100 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 312 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 s6patch触摸/0001-focaltech-msm-drm-notifier.patch
 create mode 100644 s6patch触摸/README.md

